            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "north-western Europe",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "In the northern hemisphere, robust response patterns are the slight weakening of the low pressure systems over the Aleutians and in the North Atlantic. However, in the latter region only a tiny patch southwest of Iceland is robustly positive, and the single models predict fairly different locations of the centers of their high pressure anomalies (not shown). This means that fairly different responses of the North-Atlantic Oscillation (NAO) and north-western European climate are simulated in the different ESMs.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
